INTRO(3)

NAME
     intro - the AZ/UX C library

DESCRIPTION
     /usr/lib/libc.a provides the standard C library and the POSIX
     calls a small UNIX needs. Headers are in /usr/include:

     <assert.h> <ctype.h> <errno.h> <float.h> <inttypes.h> <iso646.h>
     <limits.h> <locale.h> <math.h> <setjmp.h> <signal.h> <stdarg.h>
     <stdbool.h> <stddef.h> <stdint.h> <stdio.h> <stdlib.h> <string.h>
     <strings.h> <time.h> <dirent.h> <fcntl.h> <grp.h> <libgen.h>
     <pwd.h> <termios.h> <unistd.h> <sys/ioctl.h> <sys/stat.h>
     <sys/syscall.h> <sys/time.h> <sys/times.h> <sys/types.h>
     <sys/utsname.h> <sys/wait.h>

     Highlights
       stdio     buffered FILE streams (line buffered on terminals),
                 printf/scanf families with floating point, getline,
                 popen/pclose, tmpfile
       stdlib    malloc/calloc/realloc/free, strtol/strtod and friends,
                 qsort, bsearch, rand, getenv/setenv, system, mkstemp,
                 realpath, atexit
       string    the str* and mem* functions, strtok_r, strdup,
                 strerror, strsignal
       math      the 68882 provides sqrt, sin, cos, tan, the inverse
                 and hyperbolic functions, exp, log, log10, log2; pow,
                 floor, ceil, round, fmod, frexp, ldexp, modf, hypot,
                 cbrt and the classification macros are also available
       unistd    the system calls, exec*, getopt, sleep/usleep
       time      time, gmtime/localtime (UTC), mktime, strftime
       other     setjmp/longjmp, signal/sigaction, opendir/readdir,
                 tcgetattr/tcsetattr, getpwnam/getgrnam

     Sources are in /usr/src/libc.

SEE ALSO
     cc(1), intro(2)
